cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "backtest-bias: survivorship and integrity checks for financial price panels"
message: "If you use this software or the measured constants in the Bias Table, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jain
    given-names: Ayan
    website: "https://finance-broski.github.io/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Finance-broski/backtest-bias"
url: "https://finance-broski.github.io/"
abstract: >-
  A Python library that tests whether a financial price panel is survivorship-correct, together
  with the Indian Backtest Bias Table: a set of measured bias constants for Indian equities
  covering survivorship, index-membership look-ahead, fundamentals announcement lag, cost
  non-stationarity and marking frequency. Verdicts quote measured effect sizes rather than
  assumed ones, benchmarked against a point-in-time reference panel of 3,800+ symbols with
  1,190+ delisted names.
keywords:
  - backtesting
  - survivorship bias
  - look-ahead bias
  - point-in-time data
  - quantitative finance
  - Indian equities
  - data quality
license: MIT
version: 0.1.2
date-released: "2026-08-01"
